#!/usr/bin/python3
"""exteriqctl — install, operate, upgrade and recover a native Exteriq ASM installation.

Supported target: Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (amd64). Standard library only, so it keeps working
when a release, the database or the broker is broken.

Layout
  /opt/exteriq/releases/<version>/   one immutable release each (package exteriq-release-<version>)
  /opt/exteriq/current               symlink to the active release
  /etc/exteriq/                      configuration and secrets (never printed)
  /var/lib/exteriq/                  data: storage, exports, broker, backups, diagnostics
  /var/log/exteriq/                  categorized JSON logs (written by rsyslog only)

Every command is idempotent: re-running `install` after a failure continues where it
stopped. Nothing here deletes data except `restore` (after a safety dump) and
`purge-data --yes-delete-all-data`.
"""

